From: zhanghaotian <zhanghaotian@uniontech.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:43:58 +0800
Subject: fix: modesetting: Do not rotate damage clips in the shared pixmap
 path

Rotated outputs driven through the slave-GPU shared/prime pixmap path
(dispatch_dirty_pixmap, used by drmModeDirtyFB based displays such as
udl/evdi USB displays) show black or stale regions on the panel.

In dispatch_dirty_pixmap() the damage rectangles are already expressed
in the scanout framebuffer's own coordinate space: the shared/prime
pixmap, whose content already carries the CRTC rotation. Feeding them
through rotate_clip() with crtc->rotation transposes them out of the
framebuffer bounds for non-square (portrait/landscape) buffers. The
kernel damage iterator (drm_atomic_helper_damage_iter_next) then
intersects the out-of-bounds clip with the plane src, so only part of
the scanout is ever transferred. On a DisplayLink (udl) at 800x1280
rotated 90 degrees the full-screen damage (0,0,800,1280) becomes the
out-of-bounds (0,0,1280,800), is clipped to (0,0,800,800), and the
bottom 480 rows of the panel are never painted, showing as a black band
when the panel is used rotated.

Pass the rotation to dispatch_dirty_region() explicitly: the primary
screen path (dispatch_dirty) keeps crtc->rotation, because there the
damage is in screen coordinates and the scanout fb is a rotated shadow
buffer; the shared pixmap path (dispatch_dirty_pixmap) passes
RR_Rotate_0 so its fb-space clips are forwarded unchanged.

Signed-off-by: zhanghaotian <zhanghaotian@uniontech.com>
---
 hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/driver.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/driver.c b/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/driver.c
index fe3315a..8a149d7 100644
--- a/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/driver.c
+++ b/hw/xfree86/drivers/modesetting/driver.c
@@ -549,7 +549,8 @@ rotate_clip(PixmapPtr pixmap, BoxPtr rect, drmModeClip *clip, Rotation rotation)
 
 static int
 dispatch_dirty_region(ScrnInfoPtr scrn, xf86CrtcPtr crtc,
-		      PixmapPtr pixmap, DamagePtr damage, int fb_id)
+		      PixmapPtr pixmap, DamagePtr damage, int fb_id,
+		      Rotation rotation)
 {
     modesettingPtr ms = modesettingPTR(scrn);
     RegionPtr dirty = DamageRegion(damage);
@@ -566,7 +567,7 @@ dispatch_dirty_region(ScrnInfoPtr scrn, xf86CrtcPtr crtc,
 
         /* Rotate and copy rects into clips */
         for (i = 0; i < num_cliprects; i++, rect++)
-	    rotate_clip(pixmap, rect, &clip[i], crtc->rotation);
+	    rotate_clip(pixmap, rect, &clip[i], rotation);
 
         /* TODO query connector property to see if this is needed */
         ret = drmModeDirtyFB(ms->fd, fb_id, clip, num_cliprects);
@@ -604,7 +605,8 @@ dispatch_dirty(ScreenPtr pScreen)
 
 	drmmode_crtc_get_fb_id(crtc, &fb_id, &x, &y);
 
-        ret = dispatch_dirty_region(scrn, crtc, pixmap, ms->damage, fb_id);
+        ret = dispatch_dirty_region(scrn, crtc, pixmap, ms->damage, fb_id,
+                                    crtc->rotation);
         if (ret == -EINVAL || ret == -ENOSYS) {
             ms->dirty_enabled = FALSE;
             DamageUnregister(ms->damage);
@@ -625,7 +627,15 @@ dispatch_dirty_pixmap(ScrnInfoPtr scrn, xf86CrtcPtr crtc, PixmapPtr ppix)
     DamagePtr damage = ppriv->secondary_damage;
     int fb_id = ppriv->fb_id;
 
-    dispatch_dirty_region(scrn, crtc, ppix, damage, fb_id);
+    /* Damage rectangles in this path are expressed in the scanout
+     * framebuffer's own coordinate space (the shared/prime pixmap), whose
+     * content already carries any CRTC rotation. Converting them with
+     * rotate_clip() would transpose them out of the fb's bounds for
+     * non-square (portrait/landscape) framebuffers, so that e.g. the udl
+     * DisplayLink driver only ever transfers part of the scanout. Pass
+     * RR_Rotate_0 so the clip rectangles are forwarded unchanged.
+     */
+    dispatch_dirty_region(scrn, crtc, ppix, damage, fb_id, RR_Rotate_0);
 }
 
 static void
